Coaster Capital Update: Legend Cards
This update adds a new rare-card system to Coaster Capital, giving the auction deck bigger moments, higher stakes, and more long-term strategy.
The game now includes Legend Gold Cards, special ultra-rare attraction cards that are more powerful than normal cards and come with unique abilities. These cards are designed to feel like major auction events, not just another attraction being added to the park board.
Only two Legend cards exist in the game:
Golden Comet, 1928
A legendary wooden coaster built around massive nostalgia and long-term legacy value. Golden Comet gives its owner bonus legacy at the end of each season, making it valuable even when it is not the featured attraction.
The Lost Mill
A legendary dark ride with a special scoring advantage. The Lost Mill counts as both a Dark Ride and a Historic card for bonuses, making it useful across multiple event types and especially strong during heritage-focused seasons.
Legend cards now have their own gold visual style, making them stand out immediately when they appear in the auction. The AI also values them more highly, so bidding on a Legend card should feel more competitive and risky.
To keep the game balanced, Legend cards cannot appear in Season 1. Starting in Seasons 2 through 5, each auction has a chance to pull an unused Legend card, but they remain rare. Since there are only two in the whole deck, each Legend card can only appear once per game.
Overall, the Legend Card update adds a chase-card system to Coaster Capital, giving players something exciting to watch for while adding more tension, strategy, and reward to the auction table.
